  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "MACE: Preliminary Results of the Eastern Bering Sea EIT Pollock Survey",
  "description": "The MACE Program conducted an echo integration-trawl (EIT) survey of walleye pollock between 4 June and 30 July 2002 on the eastern Bering Sea shelf. The principal objective of the survey was to collect echo integration and trawl data to estimate midwater pollock abundance and distribution. Acoustic data were collected with Simrad EK500 and EK60 quantitative echo-sounding systems on the NOAA ship Miller Freeman. AFSC Quarterly Report: Jul. - Sep. 2002\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect echo integration and trawl data to estimate midwater pollock abundance and distribution.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23509714",
